      "functional_impact_measured": "Live (non-permeabilized) anti-FLAG labeling confirmed surface display of FLAG at position 277; PAC-FLAG_277 functioned as a quantitative reporter of surface PAC levels in an endocytosis assay \u2014 Y10A and L13A mutants showed stronger plasma membrane FLAG signal than WT, consistent with regulated endocytosis of the tagged channel.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "L1 explicitly names position 277 as the FLAG insertion site in the extracellular loop of full-length human PAC expressed in stable HEK293 cells. Python confirms residue 277 (S) falls within the extracellular span 86\u2013301, is 192 residues from TM1 end and 25 residues from TM2 start, satisfying the \u22653-residue TM-clearance constraint. L2 and L3 provide additional validation: live-cell (non-permeabilized) labeling confirmed surface exposure of the FLAG epitope, and the construct served as a functional endocytosis reporter, establishing that the tag does not disrupt trafficking or surface expression. Stable inducible HEK293 cell lines expressing full-length human PAC with FLAG inserted at position 277 in the extracellular loop (PAC-FLAG_277); live (non-permeabilized) anti-FLAG immunostaining confirmed surface display; construct used as functional reporter in endocytosis assay comparing WT vs. Y10A/L13A endocytosis-deficient mutants.",
